  "query_preview": "..Gusty west to northwest winds remain across the\nregion this afternoon. Northwesterly flow associated with an \nactive northern stream remains in place. High pressure will \ngradually shift into the Great Basin Thursday. These gusty \nnorthwest winds and dry conditions will bring critical fire \nweather conditions to much of central, eastern and southern Utah \nthrough Wednesday. See the fire weather discussion for more \ndetails.\n\nAs a shortwave trough shifts eastward into the Great Basin Friday,\nexpect gusty southwesterly winds to develop across much of the\nregion. Currently, the threat of wind advisory winds (gusts 45\nmph+) is around 30% or so across west central and southwest Utah\nFriday afternoon into Friday evening. A mainly dry cold front will\ncross into Utah Friday evening...which may prolong the period of\ngusty winds into the first part of Friday night.\n\nIsolated high-based convection will be possible as early as\nThursday across the southern mountains...and then across northern\nUtah in association with the shortwave trough Friday into\nSaturday. By Saturday, sufficient instability and deep layer shear\nmay exist across northern Utah to bring a threat of organized\nconvection. Something to monitor moving forward.",
